ontract [1], for 14,340 euros, was awarded in December 2025. Contract [2], for 14,568.45 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts in December does not indicate improper activity. Similar trends could result from seasonal demand or budget cycles. Small amounts near the limit do not prove violations, as prices may vary or budgets may be fixed.\nWhat can be checked: Check the contract dates and awardees for consistency. Review the specific services purchased in December to ensure they align with the body's needs. Examine if multiple contracts cover the same service to identify potential overlaps or repeated purchases.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["9bhZwsGiI%2F8kJPJS%2BPS9vg%3D%3D","LCQ6IsgfVKzyoM4us5k4vw%3D%3D","F2vMPc0d1Ynua%2Fi14w%2FPLA%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-16"}}